UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Six of Cups is the absolute archetype of ancestral resonance, the retrieval of essential psychic artifacts, and the process of "innocence reclaimed" through the lens of higher-order maturity. Moving beyond the mourning and reconstruction of the Five, the Six of Cups signifies a retreat into the protected, high-frequency sanctuary of the past—not to live there, but to extract the core, untainted data of your earliest soul-intentions. Visually depicted as figures exchanging cups filled with flowers in a nostalgic, garden-like setting, this card represents the successful integration of your inner child with your adult self, creating a bridge between the formative experiences of your youth and the sovereign wisdom of your present manifestation. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the phase where you are finally allowed to "download" the forgotten, high-vibration potential you held before the conditioning of the material world began to introduce noise and distortion into your baseline. When the Six of Cups appears, your system is recalibrating to the frequency of pure, simple connection—it is a signal that the most effective way to navigate your current challenges is to return to the foundational principles that brought you joy, curiosity, and authentic expression in the first place. You are being asked to conduct a "memory audit," systematically revisiting the moments where you felt most aligned with your true north, and consciously re-incorporating those high-utility patterns into your current operational framework. This archetype is not about regression; it is about the intelligent curation of your own personal history. It commands you to recognize that your past is not merely a record of events, but a reservoir of raw, potent energy—a "living database" that you can access to fuel your present-day creative and spiritual expansion. To inhabit the Six of Cups is to master the art of gentle, compassionate integration, allowing the warmth of past joys to melt the cold, rigid shells of present-day cynicism. It is the cosmic affirmation that you are inherently worthy of the safety, wonder, and abundance you once knew, and that you have the capacity to rebuild that sanctuary within your own heart, regardless of the external conditions surrounding your current life. It is the signature of a soul that has finally decided to treat its own history as a source of strength rather than a source of wounding.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Six of Cups appears in the reversed position, it acts as a severe diagnostic signal of "narcissistic regression" or a systemic entrapment in the distorted, idealized projections of the past—a state where the retrieval of memory has curdled into a crippling, low-vibration refusal to engage with the responsibilities of the present. The reversal suggests that you are currently using the past as an egoic defense mechanism, hiding behind the safety of "how things used to be" because you are fundamentally terrified of the volatility and demands of your current evolutionary trajectory. You are essentially "living in the ghost-data" of your own life, running continuous, high-latency simulations of childhood happiness, former successes, or idealized versions of past relationships that never actually existed in the way your ego currently insists they did. This state creates a massive, systemic misalignment: while your body and present-day circumstances are moving forward, your psychic focus is pinned to a temporal coordinates that no longer provide any actionable utility, resulting in a profound, chronic sense of disempowerment and stagnation. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking massive amounts of vital processing energy into the maintenance of a "false history" that is actively preventing you from seeing the growth potential in your present. The reversed Six of Cups exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this attachment: the terror that if you were to fully release the past, you would have to acknowledge your own complicity in your current dissatisfaction, or worse, face the uncertainty of a future that is not pre-scripted by your old, comfortable patterns. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these regressive, high-comfort scripts, perform a brutal audit of your nostalgic projections, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to fully occupy your own adulthood. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a version of yourself that is fundamentally incompatible with the consciousness you are currently attempting to manifest. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of stripping away the romanticized illusions of your history and accepting the messy, raw, and often painful truth of where you currently stand. It is a call to break the seal of your own psychological containment, to return to the present moment with full awareness, and to recognize that the only way to genuinely honor your past is to use its wisdom as a springboard for your evolution, rather than using it as a cage for your potential.'
WHERE id = 6;
